      "id": 1,
      "text": "New Vienna was founded by German settlers with help from the Emperor of Austria, and the town was renamed in honor of Vienna.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://newviennaheritagehousemuseum.org/new-vienna"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Saint Boniface Catholic Church, the town’s oldest church, was built to serve the families who founded New Vienna.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Vienna%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The church houses a rare late‑19th‑century William Schuelke pipe organ, one of only a few original Schuelke organs left.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Vienna%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The New Vienna Historical Society runs the Heritage House Museum at 7396 Columbus St., preserving the town’s early history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
